2. FILES CARRYING THIRD-PARTY LICENCE OBLIGATIONS

  The files below are adapted from third-party sources. Their licences are
  reproduced obligations, not a choice made here, and they attach only to the
  files named. Aggregating them in this repository does not place anything in
  section 1 under those licences: this repository is a collection, not an
  adaptation of its own contents.

  Full credits, the licence links, and a statement of what was changed are in
  ATTRIBUTION.txt.

  (a) Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
      Adapted from English Wiktionary:

        data/words/**
        data/wordlist.csv          (headword column; the frequency and tier
                                    columns are derived from wordfreq, MIT)
        data/roots/**              (see also (c))
        data/roots-manifest.csv
        data/loans/**
        data/loans-manifest.csv
        data/classifiers/**        (except the records noted below)
        data/classifiers-manifest.csv
        data/classifier-rules.json (except the rules noted below)
        data/minimal-pairs/**
        data/minimal-pairs-tone-manifest.csv
        data/minimal-pairs-vowel-manifest.csv
        data/bare-pairs/**
        data/bare-pairs-manifest.csv
        the records with ids beginning "wikt-" in data/sentences/**
        and data/sentences-manifest.json

      The classifier files are mixed. English Wiktionary records a classifier
      only on some nouns, and unevenly by semantic family rather than by
      frequency, so a second source was written to fill the gap. Records in
      data/classifiers/** carrying "source": "curated" or "curated-gloss",
      and the classifier rules they introduce in data/classifier-rules.json,
      are original to this repository, are not adapted from Wiktionary, and
      are therefore under section 1 rather than CC BY-SA. The "source" field
      ships precisely so the two can be told apart. See
      dataraw/classifier/curated/README.md.

      dataraw/root-sino/CEDICT_EVAL.md also quotes glosses from CC-CEDICT,
      a separate CC BY-SA 4.0 source (see ATTRIBUTION.txt), for comparison.
      Nothing in it feeds data/roots/** or any other shipped file.

  (b) Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France (CC BY 2.0 FR)
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/
      From Tatoeba:

        the records with ids beginning "tatoeba-" in data/sentences/**
        and data/sentences-manifest.json

  (c) Unicode Licence v3
      https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
      The character readings and glosses taken from the Unicode Unihan
      database, as they appear within data/roots/**; and the emoji names
      taken from Unicode CLDR's emoji annotations, together with the emoji
      grouping taken from Unicode's emoji-test.txt:

        data/emoji/**
        data/emoji-manifest.csv

      The required copyright and permission notice is reproduced in
      ATTRIBUTION.txt.

  (d) Public domain
      The Vietnamese source texts in data/verse/** and data/prose/**:
      Truyện Kiều (Nguyễn Du, d. 1820), Chí Phèo (Nam Cao, 1941), Hà Nội băm
      sáu phố phường (Thạch Lam, 1943), and the Universal Declaration of Human
      Rights in Vietnamese (UN General Assembly resolution 217 A (III), an
      official UN document). Each file states its own provenance and the
      reasoning for its public-domain status.

  (e) All rights reserved
      The English translations in data/verse/** and data/prose/**. They were
      generated from the public-domain Vietnamese texts above and are not
      derived from any copyleft or third-party material, so no licence
      obligation reaches them. They are machine translations; see
      ATTRIBUTION.txt before relying on them for anything.

  (f) SIL Open Font License 1.1
      https://openfontlicense.org
      Subsets of Google's Noto Emoji and Noto Color Emoji, cut to the glyphs
      the emoji card type uses:

        data/fonts/NotoEmoji-subset.woff2
        data/fonts/NotoColorEmoji-flags.woff2

      Neither original declares a Reserved Font Name, so the subsets keep the
      Noto names. Both licences, with their copyright notices, are reproduced
      in data/fonts/OFL.txt, which the OFL requires to travel with them.


